atlas apps
# The nine Frappe apps as first-class wired organs -- projections over shared
# semantic objects, not separate destinations. Each declares the mature powers it
# donates into the fabric (owns/publishes) and the fabric facts it reads
# (consumes), per the wiring riff SS5. The Frappe apps are REAL installed products
# under integrations/frappe-bench/apps (hundreds of DocTypes each, extracted by
# cmd/BonfyreFrappeCompiler) -- maturity implemented, each app fact grounded in a
# real DocType. The native compiler now reads installed DocType JSON directly;
# the remaining wiring per app is the runtime write-back of its facts into
# fabric.db. `atlas.mjs wiring` shows which
# app<->fabric feedback loops close (CRM<->actor, HRMS<->work, ERPNext<->provider).

architecture frappe-core
  canonical_name FrappeCore
  family apps
  domain Apps / Platform
  layer surface
  semantic_question What DocType, form, permission and workflow grammar does a record present?
  purpose Donates DocType schemas, forms, permissions, workflows, reports. Shapes records; it never owns the authority that gates them.
  maturity implemented
  source_path integrations/frappe-bench/apps/frappe
  source_path lib/libbonfyre/src/bonfyre_frappe_compiler.c
  witness cmd/BonfyreFrappeCompiler/tests/native_schema_ingest_smoke.sh
  witness cmd/BonfyreFrappeCompiler/tests/cms_status_roundtrip_test.sh compiles the real ToDo status, creates and updates a native CMS record, refuses an alias collision without replacing the output, and withholds conditions that still read the donor name
  invariant a donor status is projected as frappe_status with an explicit source alias; CMS publication status stays separate, and donor-status conditions are withheld until translated
  known_gap status values are carried with their donor enumeration metadata; the CMS write owner does not yet enforce those enumeration values, and no Frappe controller or remote write follows
  owns DocType
  consumes Authority
  publishes SurfaceGrammar
  publishes Policy
  forbidden_inference a DocType exists -> the record is authorized (Authority gates; a DocType only shapes)
  source_lineage aurekai institution vision (9 Frappe apps as one institutional graph)
  invariant the lineage registry is declared in architecture/apps/app-lineages.contract.yaff and generated; it was a C table inside the compiler, which made the set of application grammars answerable only by building a binary
  invariant a lineage records the dialect its grammar was first extracted from; Frappe is that provenance for all nine and is not the type of an application lineage, the same distinction that kept Upper90 a real institution without making it the type of every delegated one
  forbidden_inference a declared lineage -> a running application (none of the nine is installed on the serving estate; the bench exists only on a workstation)
  witness cmd/BonfyreAtlas/bonfyre-atlas compile-contracts app-lineages --check, and the generated catalogue is byte-identical to the hardcoded table it replaced
  internal_calculus compiled DocType metadata lowers to InteractionFingerprints: a bounded vector of evidenced generic grammars (record form, grid, lifecycle board, timeline, calendar, correspondence, relationship inspector, composition table, editor, preview, spatial or progression). This is a renderer-selection input, not a clone of a Frappe screen.
  invariant an InteractionFingerprint is extracted from parsed fields and record posture; it does not use application-name branches to manufacture an interaction grammar
  cannot_infer an InteractionFingerprint -> a Frappe controller, permission, document, runtime, authority, effect right or a requirement to reproduce a donor interface
  known_gap native phase-one extraction produces metadata grammar only; runtime write-back and controller/effect admission remain separate owners

architecture frappe-interaction-fingerprint
  canonical_name FrappeInteractionFingerprint
  family apps
  domain Apps / Measured interaction grammar
  layer surface
  semantic_question Which generic human interaction grammars does one compiled DocType actually evidence?
  purpose The native Frappe compiler extracts a reproducible vector from parsed field types, labels and record posture. It lets a Bonfyre renderer recognize kanban, timeline, calendar, correspondence, relationship, composition, editor, file-preview, spatial and progression affordances without importing Frappe UI code or hardcoding an application page family.
  maturity measured
  source_path cmd/BonfyreFrappeCompiler/src/main.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreFrappeCompiler/tests/native_schema_ingest_smoke.sh
  consumes DocType
  publishes DerivedView
  invariant fingerprint roles are derived from parsed metadata and record posture, not application-name branches
  invariant the fingerprint is renderer-selection evidence only and owns neither document state nor a controller/effect boundary
  cannot_infer an interaction fingerprint -> a Frappe runtime, controller, permission, document, authority, effect right or donor implementation requirement
  witness cmd/BonfyreFrappeCompiler/tests/native_schema_ingest_smoke.sh emits valid CRM fingerprints whose every row carries the controller/permission boundary
  witness 2026-09-26 the bridge exists: the same parse now also emits a surface program per DocType, the composer reads it out of a store, and the organ a field needs is named from the field's own kind rather than chosen by a renderer
  interacts fingerprints-select-no-renderer

interaction fingerprints-select-no-renderer
  source frappe-interaction-fingerprint
  destination frappe-surface-program
  relation evidences
  preserves the fingerprint as renderer-selection evidence only: it names grammars a DocType can support and selects nothing
  drops any path by which naming a grammar could commit the estate to reproducing the donor's page
  forbidden_inference a grammar named -> a page that must exist, or a donor interface this estate owes anybody
  witness 2026-09-26 both are emitted from one parse of the same 1,152 DocTypes; the fingerprint names grammars, the surface program names layout and fields, and neither writes the other

architecture frappe-surface-program
  canonical_name FrappeSurfaceProgram
  family apps
  domain Apps / What a compiled record kind looks like
  layer surface
  semantic_question A DocType was parsed in full. What does a reader actually get shown, and which of its fields will this estate refuse?
  purpose The layout a DocType states about itself -- tabs, sections, columns -- with every field carrying the generic presentation it asks for, the client organ that answers it, and the reason it is withheld when it is. Emitted both as JSON and into a store the composer queries, and rendered natively at /s/apps/<app> and /s/record-kind/<slug>.
  maturity measured
  node_types SurfaceProgram
  node_types FieldPresentation
  edge_types laid_out_as
  internal_calculus the compiler always parsed this and then published a list of names. "surface:crm/CRM Notification", forty-four times: every tab and section break, every field kind, every mandatory flag and every link target was dropped at the last step, and a renderer handed only a name has to invent all of it. Inventing it is how a compiled application turns back into a hand-written page
  internal_calculus a field's presentation is generic and the estate's own -- prose, money, reference, composition, place -- never a Frappe fieldtype leaked into a page, because the presentation is what a reader sees and the fieldtype is what the donor stored
  internal_calculus most fields need no script, and the emitter says so: an organ named where none is required is how a page acquires a script it never uses. Only a child table and a geolocation name one
  internal_calculus a refused field is named with its reason rather than omitted, because a field missing from a page and a field this estate will not show are different facts
  internal_calculus a tab empty in the metadata is recorded as empty rather than disappearing: the donor's client fills it at run time and this estate does not run that client
  internal_calculus what a record kind reaches into is read off its own fields -- amounts mean it carries a price, submittable means an act that binds, a field naming a student or guardian means it reaches into a household -- so the cross-links are derived and not decoration
  invariant a program is the shape of a record and never a record: no document of any of these kinds exists in this estate
  invariant a password field is never emitted with a presentation, and a button is named as an action somebody may take rather than wired to one
  invariant every field of a DocType appears exactly once, as rendered or as withheld; the counts are checked against the layout
  forbidden_inference a surface program -> a Frappe runtime, controller, permission, saved document or effect right
  forbidden_inference a rendered layout -> that this estate can read or write records of that DocType anywhere
  forbidden_inference a field marked required -> a validation this estate performs; it is the donor's statement about its own records
  source_path cmd/BonfyreFrappeCompiler/src/main.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/main.c
  source_path site/matrix/client-organs.js
  witness 2026-09-26 nine applications compiled: 1,152 DocTypes, 17,003 fields resolved as 12,459 with a stated presentation, 154 withheld with the reason, and 4,390 layout breaks that the previous output discarded entirely
  witness 2026-09-26 withheld for stated reasons and no others: 107 buttons because a donor button invokes that donor's controller, 43 password fields because a secret is never rendered here, and 4 fields that frappe's own new-doctype-1 and new-doctype-2 gave a label and no name
  witness 2026-09-26 organs are named only where a field asks for one: 298 DocTypes need the virtualised list, 3 need the spatial index, and the remaining 851 need no script at all
  witness 2026-09-26 served natively: /s/apps/crm renders 44 record kinds in one virtualised list, and /s/record-kind/crm-crm-lead renders all nine tabs of CRM Lead -- including the two that are empty in the metadata, each naming why -- with 3 money fields, 3 child tables and 1 household-facing field derived as what it reaches into
  internal_calculus who would recognise a record kind is a declared pairing, not a resemblance. An archetype is offered only where a property the compiler measured off the fields is actually present, and naming somebody is recognition rather than permission
  invariant an affinity may only require one of the five properties the compiler measures, and a sixth cannot appear without the build refusing
  invariant a fieldname reaches into a household only as a whole underscore-separated segment of a declared name; a substring test is forbidden in the source and the build asserts its absence
  forbidden_inference an archetype named beside a record kind -> a role anybody holds, permission to act on one, or a record of that kind held here for anyone
  source_path schemas/control/operators.cue
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tools/compile_operators.zig
  witness 2026-09-26 fifteen affinities declared in CUE bind eleven archetypes to the five measured properties, and the record-kind room names them from the fields: Sales Invoice offers the PTA officer, room parent, club admin, marketplace seller, deal curator, forum maintainer, supported creator and newsletter writer, each with the reason declared and its own cannot-infer
  witness 2026-09-26 the household test was wrong three ways and measurement caught all three. Asking whether a fieldname contained the word made CRM Lead reach into a household through no_of_employees, a dropdown for company size; it would have made every Frappe child row's parent into somebody's parent (57 fields); and "member" is club membership in every app that has it (63). Declared names matched as whole segments left one candidate, erpnext's price_not_uom_dependent, which withdrew the declared name "dependent" as well
  witness 2026-09-26 the honest measured result across all 1,152 record kinds: none reaches into a household. LMS comes closest with a show_students setting and a member_type whose options include "Student", neither of which is a person's record -- the same finding as the frontier's, where no roster or student-record plane appears anywhere either
  known_gap the store holds what the compiler last wrote and carries no source revision per program, so a reader cannot tell which commit of an application a layout came from
  witness 2026-09-26 the tenth application was not a compile bug. bonfyre_erpnext, the estate's own overlay, is a tree of empty directories and .DS_Store files with no DocType JSON anywhere in it. The compiler knew that and said "No Frappe DocType metadata was found beneath the app path" into a list nobody printed, while the caller reported "error code: -2" -- so the refusals are now written to stderr as they happen, because a refusal nobody can read is indistinguishable from a crash
  known_gap bonfyre_erpnext holds no DocType of its own, so the estate's own overlay contributes no record kind; whether it should is a question about the overlay and not about the compiler
  known_gap the generated contracts were prerequisites of nothing. Nine of the twelve headers were listed against the binary and the governance grammar, the institution planes and the operator affinities were not, so changing one left the running server compiled against the old one -- measured here, where a withdrawn household name stayed in the binary after the header had dropped it. The build now depends on every generated header, and that is a whole class of silent staleness that was only found by checking the bytes
  interacts record-kinds-offer-the-operator-grammar

interaction record-kinds-offer-the-operator-grammar
  source frappe-surface-program
  destination project-primitive
  relation recognised_by
  preserves the archetype as a population this estate is for, never a role anybody holds here and never an authority
  drops any path by which naming somebody beside a record kind could become permission to act on one
  forbidden_inference an archetype offered -> a role granted, a record held, or an institution agreeing to anything
  witness 2026-09-26 the pairing is declared in CUE and evidenced by the compiler: an archetype appears only where a property measured off that DocType's own fields is present, and the build refuses a sixth property nobody measures
  binding schemas/control/operators.cue
