architecture frappe-condition-plan
  canonical_name FrappeConditionPlan
  family apps
  domain Apps / When a compiled record kind shows, requires, locks or folds a field
  layer surface
  semantic_question A DocType says a field depends on something. Under the donor's own semantics, what exactly does it depend on, which fields can change the answer, and which declarations are outside what this estate can evaluate?
  purpose The four donor properties that carry a condition -- depends_on, mandatory_depends_on, read_only_depends_on, collapsible_depends_on -- compiled into one source-preserving plan per distinct expression, with every declaring field kept as a use bound to that plan and every field a plan reads kept as an edge to the uses it can change. A declaration outside the supported operations is kept with the operation it is missing.
  maturity measured
  node_types ConditionPlan
  node_types ConditionUse
  edge_types read_by
  internal_calculus the donor evaluates a condition three ways and they disagree: a bare string is a field lookup where an empty list is absent, eval: is a JavaScript expression where an empty list is true, and fn: triggers a client script. The first two are compiled under exactly those rules and the third is refused by name, because one permissive evaluator would be right about none of them
  internal_calculus a plan is a body and a use is a binding. Event repeats one condition across seven weekday fields; that is one plan with seven uses, and the read edges say a change to repeat_on reaches those seven and a change to color reaches none
  internal_calculus the source is preserved where it is probably a defect. `doc.report_type=="Report Builder" || "Custom Report"` is always true and a bare `doc.icon` is a lookup of a field called "doc.icon" and always false; both compile as written and are reported as constant rather than repaired
  internal_calculus the missing-operation report is the backlog: seven declarations wait on one ERPNext inventory predicate and four on an array callback, which is a different statement from twenty-two adapters remaining
  invariant every declaration is exactly one of compiled or refused with a named missing operation; the counts are checked against the uses
  invariant loose and strict equality, in_list, includes and indexOf stay distinct operations in the plan text
  invariant where the donor expression would throw -- a member of an absent value, an unbound parent or environment value -- evaluation refuses with the reason and returns no boolean
  forbidden_inference a compiled plan -> a validation this estate performs, or a permission; it is the donor's client-side form rule
  forbidden_inference a condition said on a record-kind page -> a form that reacts; this estate holds no record of these kinds to edit, so the page states the rule and toggles nothing
  forbidden_inference requiredWhen enforced by the CMS -> the donor's server validation; it is this estate applying the donor's form rule to its own entries
  forbidden_inference an environment value this estate binds -> the donor client's state; developer mode off and the registered lineages are this estate's own statements
  forbidden_inference two plans of one shape -> equivalent behaviour
  forbidden_inference a result marked constant -> a correction applied; the source is kept as written
  source_path lib/libbonfyre/src/bonfyre_frappe_condition.c
  source_path lib/libbonfyre/include/bonfyre_frappe_condition.h
  source_path cmd/BonfyreFrappeCompiler/src/main.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/main.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreCMS/src/main.c
  witness cmd/BonfyreFrappeCompiler/tests/condition_plan_contract_test.sh
  witness cmd/BonfyreCMS/tests/conditional_required_test.sh
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/condition_words_held_desk_test.sh
  source_path cmd/BonfyreFrappeCompiler/tests/browser_condition_parity.mjs
  witness 2026-10-03 cmd/BonfyreFrappeCompiler/tests/browser_condition_parity.mjs in Chrome 146, headless, sandbox on, loading one local file: every compiled eval: condition of six applications evaluated by the native plan and by the donor's own evaluator form (let out = <code>; return out) with the donor's own in_list, cint, cstr and lstrip source loaded. frappe 262 conditions and 3,741 generated records, erpnext 438 and 6,065, hrms 109 and 1,388, crm 12 and 144, lms 22 and 263, helpdesk 22 and 258: 11,859 records, none disagreeing; 100 conditions withheld because they read the parent record or the estate's bindings
  witness 2026-10-03 the same run first found three disagreements, all one cause: two lists compared with == or != (doc.uom != doc.stock_uom). The browser answers by object identity and the plan refused. A list now carries where in the record it was read from, and two lists are the same only when that is the same place; the three records then agreed
  invariant in the form dialect a list or record read from a record equals only a value read from that same place in that same record; a list the expression writes equals nothing. In the server dialect two lists compare by what they hold, and that is refused rather than answered by identity
  forbidden_inference agreement with a browser on generated records -> agreement on every record, or agreement of the server-side Python dialect, which no browser evaluates
  witness 2026-10-03 the comparison extended to conditions that read the parent record, each given a generated parent and the donor's open-form global bound to it: 923 conditions and 12,693 records across the six applications (frappe 266 and 3,802, erpnext 491 and 6,828, hrms 110 and 1,398, crm 12 and 144, lms 22 and 263, helpdesk 22 and 258), none disagreeing; 10 conditions remain withheld because they read which applications are installed
  known_gap the browser comparison leaves out the 10 conditions that read an estate binding, and generates records from a fixed pool of values; a field holding a record, a date object or a number outside that pool is not exercised
  witness 2026-10-01 three consumers read one plan. The compiler writes a row per use into the store the composer queries, said in the DocType's own labels: 2,589 rows, 2,534 said as a sentence, 18 as always or never, 15 as depending on named fields or the donor's setup, 22 as a rule not evaluated here. The record-kind room for Event now reads "only when Repeat this Event is ticked and Repeat On is Weekly" on seven fields and carries no expression text
  witness 2026-10-01 the CMS enforces the same rule on write: Number Card compiled to a content type carries requiredWhen, an entry of type Document Type without a document_type is refused on create and rolled back on update, and one of type Custom without it is stored. A rule reading a field the content type does not carry, the parent, or the environment stays behind and is listed with the reason
  witness 2026-10-01 the environment has an owner: frappe.boot.developer_mode is bound to off, frappe.boot.versions to the registered lineages, cur_frm.doc to the parent document, and a name bound to nothing refuses
  witness 2026-10-01 nine applications compiled: 2,589 declarations, 2,567 compiled into 1,204 plans, 22 refused by name -- 13 on two ERPNext client predicates, 4 on array callbacks, 2 on flt whose parse depends on the number format, 2 on frappe client utilities, 1 on a computed member
  witness 2026-10-01 frappe alone: 659 declarations, 658 compiled, 325 plans, 70 shapes; Event's seven weekday fields share plan cp-0f0d69d66019c4f42abdf4764eb29857 and Dashboard Chart's chart_type is read by 14 uses
  witness 2026-10-01 eleven plans are constant and say so: six bare strings that are not field names (doc.contributed, doc.icon, doc.party_type, doc.received_amount, doc.returned_qty, doc.payment_gateway_account), `!is_expression`, a collapsible_depends_on of "1", two literal `eval:true`, and Report's `|| "Custom Report"`
  known_gap nothing in a browser re-evaluates a plan when a field changes, because no page here edits a record of these kinds; the read edges that would drive it are emitted and unconsumed
  known_gap visibility, read-only and collapse rules are stated on the page and enforced nowhere; only the mandatory rule has a store that applies it
  known_gap string comparison orders by bytes and the donor orders by UTF-16 units; they differ only for text outside the basic plane
  interacts condition-plans-state-the-rule

interaction condition-plans-state-the-rule
  source frappe-condition-plan
  destination frappe-surface-program
  relation refines
  preserves the surface program's depends_on text unchanged; the condition rows sit beside it in the same store, keyed by the same program and field
  drops any path by which a rule stated on a page could be read as the page reacting to a field change
  forbidden_inference a rule stated beside a field -> that the rendered page shows, hides, requires or locks that field accordingly
  witness 2026-10-01 both are written by one binary from one parse; the composer reads frappe_condition for each field it lays out and falls back to the DocType's own text when a store predates the table
  binding cmd/BonfyreFrappeCompiler/src/main.c
  binding cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/main.c

architecture frappe-notification-binding
  canonical_name FrappeNotificationBinding
  family apps
  domain Apps / What a donor notification becomes when nothing here sends
  layer surface
  semantic_question A DocType's application says: when this happens to a record and this holds, tell these people this. Which of that can this estate decide and write, and what does it do with the result?
  purpose A donor Notification definition bound to owners that already exist. The trigger and the Python condition are compiled; given one event and one record the binding says whether it fires, reads an address off the record where one is there, writes the subject and body by running the donor's own template -- printing, if, for, set, over the same server dialect the condition uses -- and yields a held message that the queue files once. No part of it transmits.
  maturity measured
  node_types NotificationPlan
  node_types HeldMessage
  edge_types fires_on
  internal_calculus the donor evaluates a notification's condition on its server in Python, where an empty list is false, text never equals a number, and not binds looser than a comparison. It is a second dialect over the same plan nodes, marked in the plan text, never the form dialect reused because it looked similar
  internal_calculus three kinds of trigger are decided here: something happened to a record, one field took a new value, a date on the record is a stated number of days away. A method or custom trigger is a controller hook and is refused by name
  internal_calculus a recipient is a selector first and an address second. A field yields an address only when the record holds one; a role, an assignment, or a field naming a person yields a recipient this estate cannot reach, and says why
  internal_calculus a standard notification's body is the file beside its definition, chosen by message_type, and not the message the definition carries; reading the wrong one renders a different message, which the first pass here did
  internal_calculus the template engine is one implementation over the plan nodes: a loop variable is an environment binding, a filter is a node, and a name the donor's template never defines is printed as written because that is what the donor prints
  internal_calculus where the donor consults a site or user date setting this estate states one format of its own: the ISO calendar date first so text sorts as time does, the weekday after it for the person reading, the 24-hour clock -- 2026-10-02 Fri 14:30. No zone is added, because a time stored on a record is in whatever zone the record means. A strftime pattern the template writes out is the author's own and is honoured as written
  internal_calculus where the donor links a record's name into its desk, the name is written and the link is not. No record of these kinds is held here and no desk is served, so a link would claim a page exists
  internal_calculus a method on a template variable is the last name of the path, so start.date() is date applied to start and never a function called start.date
  invariant a held message carries transmitted false in every state, and a message whose text could not be written carries no state at all
  invariant the same definition, event, record and day yield the same key, and filing it twice leaves one job
  invariant a definition switched off never fires
  invariant a hook is handed the write -- kind, event, entry, the row now and the row before -- because it runs before the write is released and cannot read it from the store
  invariant a condition reading a field the store keeps for its own use is not answered from that store's row
  forbidden_inference a held message -> a sent, delivered or read one
  forbidden_inference a recipient with an address -> somebody who knows the message exists
  forbidden_inference a notification decided here -> the donor's scheduler or document events running; the caller supplies the event and the day
  forbidden_inference a job in the queue -> authority to act on it
  forbidden_inference a composed body -> the text the donor would have sent; dates and desk links are this estate's own statements and the message says so
  forbidden_inference a time written without a zone -> a time in this estate's zone
  source_path cmd/BonfyreFrappeCompiler/src/main.c
  source_path lib/libbonfyre/src/bonfyre_frappe_condition.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreFrappeCompiler/tools/held_message_hook.sh
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/main.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreCMS/src/main.c
  witness cmd/BonfyreFrappeCompiler/tests/notification_held_message_test.sh
  witness cmd/BonfyreCMS/tests/hook_held_message_test.sh
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/condition_words_held_desk_test.sh
  witness 2026-10-01 the desk has a fifth queue, Messages written and held, counted against the queue store: with one composed message filed, a stranger is told there is one and not what it says or whom it names
  witness 2026-10-01 temporary native Auth sessions exercise the desk boundary: an anonymous reader and a free account see the held count without the subject or document; a write-scoped account sees the named row through its browser cookie; after logout that cookie sees only the count again; the queue node is byte-identical before and after the desk reads
  witness 2026-10-01 end to end through three owners: Fiscal Year compiled to a content type, a hook registered on it, an entry created by hand fires nothing, an entry with auto_created 1 leaves one held message in the queue carrying the composed body and no address, the same write presented again leaves one, and an update hands the hook the row as it stood before
  witness 2026-10-01 eight definitions across hrms, lms and erpnext: all eight decided here, five with a compiled Python condition and three with none. With only field substitution one was composed in full; with blocks, filters, indexing, range, flt and str.format three are -- Retention Bonus, Training Feedback, Material Request Receipt -- and the other five each name one call: format_value, formatdate, format_date, get_datetime, get_url
  witness 2026-10-01 with the estate's date format, datetime operations, bold and the withheld desk link, seven of eight are composed in full. Training Scheduled sets two variables, compares their dates and prints Friday, 02 Oct 2026 and 09:00 AM to 05:30 PM by its own patterns; Fiscal Year indexes and ranges over its companies and writes 2027-01-01 Fri; Exit Interview lists its interviewers. The eighth, New job alert, needs the donor site's address and is refused by name
  witness 2026-10-01 Material Request Receipt renders as the donor renders it: one table row per item received and none for the item that was not, 5 printed as 5.0 and 2.456 as 2.46, an absent company as None
  witness 2026-10-01 Exit Interview Scheduled fires one day before the record's date while it is scheduled and not cancelled, addresses the two people in its email field, names the assignees as unreachable, and does not fire a week early, after cancellation, or on Submit
  witness 2026-10-01 Retention Bonus is written whole -- subject and body from the record -- addressed to a role nobody here holds, and filed through bonfyre-queue under family held-message twice with one job to show for it
  known_gap one of eight bodies is not written: it builds a link from the donor site's address, which this estate does not hold
  known_gap dates are written in this estate's format on purpose, so those messages differ from the donor's by design; a named babel format such as medium or short is answered with the same one format
  known_gap a markdown body is rendered as markdown and not converted to HTML, and the donor converts before it renders; the two orders can differ where a template block spans a markdown construct
  known_gap flt rounds as C rounds a binary double; the donor rounds by its configured method, and the two differ on exact halves
  known_gap the store raises New and Save through its hooks; nothing asks daily, so a notification that counts days to a date fires only when a caller presents the day
  known_gap the desk counts held messages and names them to an account with write scope, and offers no act: nothing yet hands one over, withholds it or drops it, so the queue only grows
  known_gap the desk reads the store named by BONFYRE_HELD_MESSAGE_DB and no deployment names one yet
  known_gap a hook is registered by a row in the store's _hooks table; there is no command that registers one
  known_gap a content type carries no child table and keeps status for itself, so a rule reading a donor status is refused from a store row and a body listing child rows lists none
  known_gap set_property_after_alert, attachments and the non-email channels are read and not acted on
  interacts notification-decided-by-condition-plan
  interacts notification-yields-held-message
  interacts notification-filed-through-queue

interaction notification-decided-by-condition-plan
  source frappe-condition-plan
  destination frappe-notification-binding
  relation evidences
  preserves the dialect: a notification's condition is compiled as Python and a field's as the form's JavaScript, over one set of plan nodes
  drops any path by which a condition that cannot be evaluated counts as holding
  forbidden_inference a condition that holds -> a message that should be sent
  witness 2026-10-01 five notification conditions compile to plans marked py; a record that fails one yields fires false with the reason, and a condition outside the supported operations yields no answer
  binding lib/libbonfyre/src/bonfyre_frappe_condition.c

