architecture frappe-metric-plan
  canonical_name FrappeMetricPlan
  family apps
  domain Apps / What a donor card or chart asks of a store
  layer surface
  semantic_question An application ships a number on a dashboard. What exactly is it a count or sum of, narrowed how, and can a store this estate already has answer it?
  purpose A donor Number Card or Dashboard Chart compiled into one read: a function of a field over the records of one kind, narrowed by filters, grouped by a field or laid out over time. A compiled plan is answered from one table of one store, opened read only with every value bound, or refused by the name of what stands in the way: donor code, a field the store does not hold, or something the reader has not said.
  maturity measured
  node_types MetricPlan
  node_types MetricReading
  edge_types reads_from
  internal_calculus the corpus is a small vocabulary. Five functions, thirteen filter operators, the donor's named timespans, a group-by, and five intervals cover every card and chart that is not the donor running its own code
  internal_calculus a dynamic filter is an expression the donor's client evaluates. The common one asks for the reader's default company, and here that is a thing the reader says: unsaid, the metric is not answered, because a number silently taken over every company is a different number
  internal_calculus the other dynamic filters are evaluated by the same form dialect the field conditions use, with today bound to the day being asked about and the donor's client state bound empty, so an expression that falls back when no fiscal year is set falls back
  internal_calculus three refusals are kept apart because they are closed by different people: an operation this estate does not perform, a field the store does not carry, and something the reader has to say
  internal_calculus a column a store keeps for its own use is not the donor's field of the same name. A content type's status is draft or published; a donor Employee's status is Active or Left. Reading one as the other gives a number about nothing
  internal_calculus a week starts on Monday here, as ISO 8601 counts it; the donor reads the first day of the week from a site setting
  invariant every definition is exactly one of compiled or refused with a named operation
  invariant the store is opened read only, the table and field names are checked as plain identifiers, and every filter value is bound
  invariant a metric that needs the reader to say something returns no number until they do
  invariant a field the table does not hold refuses; it is never counted as zero
  forbidden_inference a compiled metric -> a number; it is answered only against a store carrying the fields it reads
  forbidden_inference a number read here -> the donor's number; the donor applies its own permissions and its own week
  forbidden_inference a number read from a store -> a fact about the world; the store holds what was written to it
  source_path cmd/BonfyreFrappeCompiler/src/main.c
  source_path lib/libbonfyre/src/bonfyre_frappe_condition.c
  witness cmd/BonfyreFrappeCompiler/tests/metric_read_test.sh
  witness 2026-10-02 the corpus across erpnext, hrms and lms: 134 definitions, 98 compiled, 36 refused by name -- 25 backed by a donor report, 4 by a method, 4 by a custom source, 3 over a child table. Nothing is refused for an operator, a timespan or an interval this estate lacks
  witness 2026-10-02 55 of the compiled metrics need the reader to say their company, and say so
  witness 2026-10-02 answered from a store: employees joining this quarter counts 2 at one company and 1 at another and refuses with none said; employees by department returns its groups largest first; incoming bills by month over the last year returns thirteen periods with the drafts left out by the definition's own filter and an empty month as zero
  witness 2026-10-02 the status collision is refused when the caller names the columns a store keeps: the same chart answers from a table whose status is the donor's and refuses from one whose status is the store's
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/main.c
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/condition_words_held_desk_test.sh compiles hrms into the surface store and serves two record-kind rooms: Job Applicant carries one line per metric read with a grouped chart said as "how many there are, for each country", Job Requisition names Time to Fill as not counted and why without the donor's method name, and a record kind nothing counts says nothing about counting
  witness cmd/BonfyreFrappeCompiler/tests/metric_read_test.sh checks the surface store carries the same definition and compiled counts as the emitted plans, and that every row is either said or refused
  invariant the record-kind room says each metric from its compiled plan in words and never shows the donor's function, method path or filter expression
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/condition_words_held_desk_test.sh keeps records of two compiled kinds in a content store and checks that a signed-in reader sees a grouped chart answered largest first, a card filtered on the donor's status refused because the store's status is its own, and a company-scoped card answered per company with no number across companies; that a stranger is told records are kept and given no number and no name from them; and that the store is byte-identical afterwards
  internal_calculus a record kind's records are read from the content type the compiler names for it (frappe_<app>_<doctype>); the definition travels in the surface store beside its plan and is handed to the compiler's reader on standard input, so the page owns no read of its own
  internal_calculus where the donor would ask the reader's company, the room asks nobody: each company the kept records name gets its own number, up to eight, and a subject room takes no parameter
  invariant a number, and any name drawn from a record, is said only to a signed-in reader
  forbidden_inference a number said on a record-kind room -> a number about every company; a company-scoped metric is answered per company or not at all
  forbidden_inference signed in -> entitled to these records under the donor's permissions; the donor's role and user permissions are not applied here
  known_gap the live content store holds no records of any compiled kind, so every live room says what would be counted and gives no number; the answered path is witnessed on a fixture store only
  known_gap any signed-in reader sees the numbers; the donor's per-role and per-user permissions are not modelled, and more than eight companies are cut off without saying so
  known_gap the desk does not carry a metric
  known_gap the caller names the columns a store keeps for itself; a store read without that list can be mis-answered where a name collides
  known_gap a content type compiled from a DocType carries no docstatus and no child table, so a metric filtered on docstatus is refused from such a store
  known_gap an average over periods is the mean of the rows in each period, as the donor computes it; a heatmap chart shape is refused
  interacts metric-filters-evaluated-by-condition-dialect

interaction metric-filters-evaluated-by-condition-dialect
  source frappe-condition-plan
  destination frappe-metric-plan
  relation evidences
  preserves the form dialect: a dynamic filter is compiled and evaluated by the same plan nodes a field condition uses
  drops a second expression evaluator for dashboards
  forbidden_inference an expression that evaluates -> the value the donor's client would have produced; the client state is bound empty here
  witness 2026-10-02 the fiscal-year fallback expression -- a template literal, a slice and today -- compiles to one plan and yields this calendar year's first and last day when no fiscal year is bound
  binding lib/libbonfyre/src/bonfyre_frappe_condition.c

